    "summary": "High‑energy Palace show with monster Dark Star jam and soaring Bird Song",
    "blurb": "The set opens with tight blues‑rock numbers before exploding into a 30‑minute Dark Star > China Cat Sunflower > The Other One > I Know You Rider sequence. Highlights include a soaring Bird Song, fiery Playing In The Band and the seamless Greatest Story Ever Told > Bertha > Promised Land medley. Jerry’s tone is pristine, Phil’s bass thunderous, and Keith adds tasteful keys throughout.",
    "review": "The September 24, 1972 Palace Theater concert captures the Dead at a creative peak. After a solid first set of blues‑rock staples – Big Railroad Blues, Cumberland Blues, Sugaree and a rousing Playing In The Band – the band launches into a second set that builds to one of the era’s most celebrated Dark Star journeys. The 30‑minute odyssey weaves through China Cat Sunflower, The Other One and lands on an inspired I Know You Rider, all powered by Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s booming bass takeover. Mid‑set highlights like Bird Song soar with crystalline guitar lines, while the Greatest Story Ever Told > Bertha > Promised Land medley showcases tight interplay and Keith’s tasteful electric piano fills. The night closes on a bright Sugar Magnolia and an exuberant One More Saturday Night, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all available soundboard sources the performance shines – crystal‑clear enough to hear every nuance despite a few brief cuts – making this Palace show a must‑listen for any Deadhead seeking high‑energy improvisation and memorable songcraft.",
